to-be-incorporated-into-paper-148 : List Word
to-be-incorporated-into-paper-148 = unlines (cons "In hyperactivity's language as the repository implements it: **Data types.** One mechanism serves every declared data type, with nothing written per type:" (cons "- moving a constructor value along a line of data types (e.g. `List A(i)`) moves each of its" (cons "  fields along its field type; this is derived from the declaration;" (cons "- a path constructor such as `loop i` must still meet its declared endpoints after moving, so the" (cons "  result is corrected by a composition that glues those endpoints back on;" (cons "- composition is generalized (Cubical Agda's `gcomp`): the tube gets the complement of its face," (cons "  carrying the transported starting value. At every closed point the tube is then total, so a" (cons "  composition never leaves a formal composition behind where nothing was to be composed: a" (cons "  composition with an empty tube is transport, transport along a constant line of a closed type" (cons "  is the identity (`transp (λ i → S1) base` is `base`), and transport along `ua not` of `true` is" (cons "  `false`;" (cons "- in a data type without path constructors, a composition whose starting value and sides are" (cons "  all one constructor goes into the fields, each composed along its type at the earlier fields'" (cons "  fillers (CCHM's rule), so `λ j → comp Nat [ j = 0 ↦ 1 , j = 1 ↦ 1 ] 1` is `λ j → 1` and a path" (cons "  field transported along `ua` is a constant path again. The machine looks at the starting value" (cons "  and then at each side at a fresh dimension; a side that is not that constructor (a variable)" (cons "  keeps the composition formal, and a substitution decides again. The checker accepts a formal" (cons "  composition in such a type only when its tube covers every closed point, as the machine's own" (cons "  do, so a closed value of such a type is a constructor;" (cons "- a composition in a data type that cannot be computed further is kept as a value, `hcompD`; a case" (cons "  analysis meeting such a value applies itself to the pieces and composes the results in the" (cons "  result type." nil))))))))))))))))))))))
